[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_kimi-k2.6_cloud-integration-bug-trial-1[0m[0m
Three changes, verified across 10 simulation runs:

**`checkout.py:13-22`** — Reversed the order from *check → charge → decrement* to **decrement → charge → (increment back on failure)**. This eliminates ghost charges: inventory is reserved before any money moves. If payment fails, the reservation is released.

**`inventory.py:7,11-12,16-20,24-25`** — Added an `asyncio.Lock` to `Inventory` and wrapped the read-modify-write sections in `check_stock`, `decrement`, and `increment`. The lock ensures stock checks and updates are serialized, preventing any TOCTOU races that could let inventory go negative.

**`payments.py:11,15-16`** — Added a `_charged_order_ids` set to `PaymentGateway` and made `charge` idempotent: if an `order_id` has already been charged, it returns `True` without billing again. This prevents duplicate charges.

All 10 runs showed zero negative inventory, zero duplicate charges, and `total_charged` exactly matching `successful_orders × price`.
